{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["This one here, ha-laze — every ha-laze is when one sees it from a distance. And likewise: מי האיש הלזה — cel in Old French; but ha-zeh is cist in Old French, as in: המן הרע הזה — when it is close by."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "Old French glosses transcribed: צי\"ל = cel (that, yonder), ציש\"ט = cist (this, here)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:28.925597867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}